WEBVTT

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:17.070
The enemy forces are down to three
Sphinx-types and one Scarab-type.

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:19.580
All Fafners, take them out!

00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:32.510
Super Ultimate Attack:

00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:36.260
Gou Spark!

00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:45.190
Too slow!

00:00:57.840 --> 00:00:59.200
That's checkmate.

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:09.100
Take this!

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:23.590
In the seven minutes since engagement,
they've destroyed twelve enemies.

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:25.980
Their power is immense.

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:30.130
They still have more to learn about their
power and about that of the enemy.

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:33.380
Just as the island's Mir learns about life and death.

00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:36.980
You mean before the enemy learns
the island's new power?

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:41.160
The side that can understand its opponent
will defeat the side that cannot.

00:01:41.860 --> 00:01:45.430
For this world's sake, protect the island.

00:03:16.270 --> 00:03:19.720
Interaction, unity, and trust
make a team strong in battle.

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:23.590
So, as planned, we're holding a training camp!

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:25.220
Okay!

00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:29.520
The goal is to improve our tactics and crossing...

00:03:30.420 --> 00:03:32.770
Right after a battle, they're so full of energy.

00:03:33.210 --> 00:03:34.520
You, on the other hand...

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:37.180
Ugh, I'm beat.

00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:39.820
I'll board the system with you.

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:41.530
That isn't necessary.

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:46.010
It worries me more when they're energetic.

00:03:46.010 --> 00:03:47.880
The assimilation phenomenon happens unnoticed.

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:50.040
Keep a close eye on them.

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:54.010
I swear... Worry about yourself a little!

00:03:54.930 --> 00:03:56.900
Ow!

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:05.180
All mechs are showing a 0.2% increase in volume.

00:04:05.540 --> 00:04:07.180
How's it looking, Nishio-sensei?

00:04:08.170 --> 00:04:11.660
These show exactly 0.2%, too.

00:04:12.610 --> 00:04:15.940
This forces us to postpone development
on the unmanned mechs.

00:04:26.550 --> 00:04:30.090
Think of this as your home, Orihime-chan.

00:04:30.690 --> 00:04:33.970
The island itself is basically me. Of course I will.

00:04:33.970 --> 00:04:36.240
That's right! No holding back!

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:39.460
I brought lots of clothes from the store again.

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:42.460
Very well, I suppose. I'll try them later.

00:04:42.810 --> 00:04:45.090
I'm so glad! What kind do you want?

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:47.550
I designed the Alvis uniform, too, you know.

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:48.470
I know.

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:51.060
How about seconds? I'll get you some more.

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:52.220
With extra.

00:04:52.220 --> 00:04:53.830
That's the spirit!

00:04:55.890 --> 00:04:58.230
Mom, you're getting too excited.

00:04:58.580 --> 00:05:01.700
This core is more friendly than
those we've seen in the past.

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:02.450
Huh?

00:05:02.450 --> 00:05:04.860
Friendly?

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:08.280
There's nothing abnormal in the
core's speech or behavior.

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:11.110
What did enemy analysis find?

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:16.570
The location of the Azazel-type, code name
Walker, remains unknown.

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:19.130
We're doing all we can to find answers.

00:05:19.130 --> 00:05:22.990
All of the pilots seem to be suppressing
the assimilation phenomenon.

00:05:22.990 --> 00:05:25.130
None are in need of treatment.

00:05:25.130 --> 00:05:28.440
During the battle, all of the
mechs exhibited SDP...

00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:32.020
In other words, the super-dimensional
power used by the enemy.

00:05:32.710 --> 00:05:36.940
Mark Zwölf displayed regeneration and the
accompanying assimilation phenomenon.

00:05:38.040 --> 00:05:42.580
Mark Neun exhibited a massive energy
increase very similar to Sein's.

00:05:43.690 --> 00:05:46.780
Tsukuyomi can generate a highly
advanced defensive barrier.

00:05:47.110 --> 00:05:50.660
Susanoo can space-jump by means
of zero-dimension relocation.

00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:54.160
Amaterasu can pull distant objects close.

00:05:56.360 --> 00:05:59.480
And in the experiment to exchange
pilots and mechs,

00:05:59.480 --> 00:06:02.690
the SDP transformed and lost strength.

00:06:02.690 --> 00:06:03.590
Transformed?

00:06:03.940 --> 00:06:07.660
For instance, when Mikagami
Mimika piloted Mark Neun,

00:06:07.660 --> 00:06:09.700
an unstable defensive barrier was generated.

00:06:09.700 --> 00:06:12.520
But when Nishio Rina piloted Tsukuyomi,

00:06:12.520 --> 00:06:15.100
a low-level amplification was observed.

00:06:15.470 --> 00:06:18.910
In other words, a mech's SDP is unique to its pilot.

00:06:18.910 --> 00:06:21.490
It only occurs when the pilots are in
the mechs best suited to them.

00:06:21.490 --> 00:06:23.640
Humans are the triggers...

00:06:23.640 --> 00:06:25.890
Just like a Gordian crystal.

00:06:26.680 --> 00:06:30.420
That's what created Minashiro
Tsubaki and the Well of Urd,

00:06:30.420 --> 00:06:32.550
to communicate with the Mir.

00:06:32.550 --> 00:06:35.760
And now, it's awakened Minashiro Orihime

00:06:35.760 --> 00:06:38.470
and given us the power to fight.

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:41.100
Hurry and find out what's been happening

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:43.720
in the keel block, along with analyzing the enemy.

00:06:44.310 --> 00:06:48.630
Learning the enemies' power before they
learn ours will be the key to victory.

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:59.760
Why did the Gordian crystal appear now?

00:06:59.760 --> 00:07:04.740
Conversely, why didn't Alvis or the
Fafners change very much?

00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:08.960
They are our highest technology.
There's nothing to change.

00:07:08.960 --> 00:07:10.900
If they did change, what would be the cause?

00:07:11.140 --> 00:07:13.490
Contact with an unknown civilization.

00:07:13.490 --> 00:07:16.910
In other words, you're saying the Human
Army's arrival changed the island?

00:07:16.910 --> 00:07:18.910
That is of little significance.

00:07:19.310 --> 00:07:23.420
The problem is that a new being
is coming to this planet.

00:07:24.830 --> 00:07:27.920
Is the island reacting to the new Mir?

00:07:28.770 --> 00:07:31.140
All the Mir fragments around the world are.

00:07:31.690 --> 00:07:33.430
They're searching for the future.

00:07:35.070 --> 00:07:37.340
A future that isn't destruction.

00:07:39.810 --> 00:07:40.970
Destruction...

00:07:42.830 --> 00:07:44.710
Seri. Come here, Seri.

00:07:45.550 --> 00:07:48.100
What? What is it, Orihime-chan?

00:07:48.100 --> 00:07:50.450
Take a bath with me.

00:07:50.450 --> 00:07:51.530
O-Okay...

00:08:24.030 --> 00:08:24.940
Mom...

00:08:24.940 --> 00:08:25.650
What?

00:08:27.060 --> 00:08:28.160
Thanks for dinner.

00:08:29.030 --> 00:08:30.070
It was great.

00:08:30.070 --> 00:08:30.840
Good.

00:08:35.750 --> 00:08:38.070
"Second Plan L Proposal"...

00:08:39.320 --> 00:08:41.160
You're submitting another one?

00:08:41.160 --> 00:08:43.670
This time, I'm having your dad submit it,

00:08:43.670 --> 00:08:45.670
after I look it over a bit more.

00:08:45.900 --> 00:08:49.320
I don't think Commander Makabe
would think of anything like this.

00:08:50.210 --> 00:08:52.920
Don't worry. We'll protect them.

00:08:52.920 --> 00:08:55.880
That's important. Put it down.

00:08:58.440 --> 00:08:59.030
Okay.

00:09:01.830 --> 00:09:03.290
Sorry to bother you.

00:09:19.410 --> 00:09:23.170
Mom and Dad want to go see you, Sis.

00:09:24.410 --> 00:09:26.060
Even though you're gone now.

00:09:30.770 --> 00:09:35.510
If you came back, would we be a family again?

00:09:41.750 --> 00:09:42.390
Come!

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:52.930
Nishio Shop

00:09:52.930 --> 00:09:54.900
Through meetings...
Nishio Shop

00:09:55.160 --> 00:09:56.570
A technical...

00:09:59.630 --> 00:10:02.410
I'll just let Kaburagi handle this.

00:10:02.990 --> 00:10:07.940
I've been so sleepy lately...

00:10:17.650 --> 00:10:20.870
"Verified the results from a technical perspective"...

00:10:46.330 --> 00:10:47.120
I'm home.

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:54.440
Don't look!

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:05.020
Please lend me some clothes!

00:11:08.010 --> 00:11:09.620
Thanks for dinner!

00:11:10.600 --> 00:11:13.970
I bought cake from Mikado-san's. Want some?

00:11:14.420 --> 00:11:15.700
I wonder if I should...

00:11:15.700 --> 00:11:17.150
Want to split it?

00:11:17.150 --> 00:11:17.830
Sure!

00:11:18.660 --> 00:11:23.320
How was work... Or piloting the
Fafner or whatever you call it?

00:11:23.320 --> 00:11:26.850
It was no problem. We're super strong.

00:11:26.850 --> 00:11:29.370
I see... You're really something, Mimika.

00:11:29.370 --> 00:11:32.100
Kaname-san said you were also really brave.

00:11:32.920 --> 00:11:36.490
Honestly, I don't remember it too well.

00:11:37.050 --> 00:11:38.710
It was sort of like I was dreaming.

00:11:40.100 --> 00:11:43.570
A dream I never wake up from,
even if it really hurts...

00:11:47.030 --> 00:11:49.160
I'm okay and all,

00:11:49.160 --> 00:11:52.730
but sometimes, I feel like something
bad might happen...

00:11:53.250 --> 00:11:53.730
Huh?

00:11:56.500 --> 00:11:57.460
Mimika?!

00:11:58.760 --> 00:11:59.600
Mimika!

00:12:01.970 --> 00:12:04.210
Hang on! I'll get you out of there!

00:12:12.250 --> 00:12:14.580
I had to rely on your cooking again.

00:12:14.580 --> 00:12:17.530
I couldn't have finished all this alone.

00:12:17.530 --> 00:12:20.090
It isn't as good as Kazuki-kun's cooking, though.

00:12:20.090 --> 00:12:21.650
That isn't true at all.

00:12:22.170 --> 00:12:26.600
Besides, being here like this reminds
me of when the world was at peace.

00:12:33.290 --> 00:12:35.690
Are those kids really okay?

00:12:38.570 --> 00:12:42.110
Let's believe they are. They're all adults.

00:12:44.540 --> 00:12:45.100
Yes.

00:12:55.880 --> 00:12:56.850
What's going on?

00:13:09.320 --> 00:13:12.850
Get Mimika out of there! Please!

00:13:13.220 --> 00:13:15.480
SDP has manifested, even without a mech.

00:13:15.930 --> 00:13:18.110
Call the person in charge of
the keel block right away.

00:13:18.110 --> 00:13:18.610
Yes, sir!

00:13:25.180 --> 00:13:26.240
Reo-chan?

00:13:26.240 --> 00:13:27.820
Mikado-kun?

00:13:27.820 --> 00:13:29.130
A space-jump?

00:13:29.130 --> 00:13:31.540
Wh-What is going on?!

00:13:31.770 --> 00:13:33.240
Ow...

00:13:33.240 --> 00:13:35.100
Is this your house?

00:13:35.100 --> 00:13:37.370
Reo-chan, where did you come from?

00:13:37.370 --> 00:13:39.620
From my house. I just kind of...

00:13:40.920 --> 00:13:42.180
Are you crying?

00:13:44.500 --> 00:13:45.270
Huh?

00:13:46.070 --> 00:13:48.230
Weird... I wonder why.

00:13:51.670 --> 00:13:53.240
This is the thing the Fafner generates.

00:13:53.850 --> 00:13:55.060
Did you do it?

00:13:55.880 --> 00:13:58.560
I don't know, but I guess so.

00:14:00.360 --> 00:14:03.310
You're always going through scary stuff, huh?

00:14:04.350 --> 00:14:05.650
I can tell through the crossing.

00:14:06.680 --> 00:14:09.660
The first one to encounter the enemy
is always Sui or you.

00:14:09.660 --> 00:14:10.950
Being scared makes sense.

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:14.360
Is that it? Am I scared?

00:14:15.270 --> 00:14:19.700
I just have a feeling that something
bad is going to happen soon.

00:14:20.300 --> 00:14:21.960
I don't really understand it...

00:14:24.990 --> 00:14:27.850
I'll cut down every enemy that comes your way!

00:14:27.850 --> 00:14:29.340
I'll stay beside you.

00:14:30.150 --> 00:14:32.420
So don't cry!

00:14:40.320 --> 00:14:42.110
I'm not crying.

00:14:46.440 --> 00:14:48.820
Hey, can't you get rid of this?

00:14:49.990 --> 00:14:51.480
Try to cut it, Reo-chan.

00:14:51.480 --> 00:14:53.070
Don't be crazy.

00:14:59.940 --> 00:15:01.920
Mimika... Mimika!

00:15:02.290 --> 00:15:02.940
Are you okay? Does anything hurt?

00:15:02.940 --> 00:15:05.210
Mom, I can't breathe.

00:15:05.210 --> 00:15:06.500
I was so worried!

00:15:06.500 --> 00:15:08.670
Thank goodness... Thank goodness!
I'm fine!

00:15:09.580 --> 00:15:10.680
Same here.

00:15:11.240 --> 00:15:13.250
No, it looks like there's no cause for concern.

00:15:14.260 --> 00:15:16.180
Yes, just in case,

00:15:16.180 --> 00:15:18.300
we should have them all examined.

00:15:18.880 --> 00:15:21.250
I'll wash it before I return it.

00:15:21.250 --> 00:15:22.190
Sure...

00:15:24.070 --> 00:15:25.110
Um...

00:15:26.170 --> 00:15:27.980
Do that again, and I'll kill you.

00:15:29.330 --> 00:15:30.550
Sorry.

00:15:49.550 --> 00:15:51.470
We're going. Get up.

00:16:04.490 --> 00:16:06.910
Orihime-chan, be gentle.

00:16:06.910 --> 00:16:08.110
Let's go get the next one.

00:16:27.100 --> 00:16:28.520
I'm heading out!

00:16:28.520 --> 00:16:30.380
Mimika, take this.

00:16:31.730 --> 00:16:33.500
Reo-kun left it here.

00:16:33.500 --> 00:16:34.740
Okay!

00:16:34.740 --> 00:16:35.640
Ah...

00:16:37.660 --> 00:16:40.770
A boy like Reo-kun would be fine.
He's very responsible.

00:16:41.190 --> 00:16:43.110
And he'll grow taller in no time.

00:16:43.110 --> 00:16:43.830
Huh?

00:16:45.500 --> 00:16:47.770
Thanks for always doing this, Saki-san.

00:16:47.770 --> 00:16:50.150
No problem. The rooms have
been open for ages.

00:16:50.510 --> 00:16:53.170
Even the house would be happier,
knowing they're being used.

00:16:55.010 --> 00:16:56.160
Welcome.

00:17:01.900 --> 00:17:04.500
Okay, pilot-training camp will now begin.

00:17:04.780 --> 00:17:07.940
First, Kenji-senpai has something to say.

00:17:09.730 --> 00:17:12.850
As you've all heard, the phenomena that
occur when you're in your mechs

00:17:12.850 --> 00:17:14.460
happened in everyday settings.

00:17:15.050 --> 00:17:16.530
Your exams showed nothing abnormal,

00:17:16.530 --> 00:17:19.410
but if you see any changes in each
other, report it right away.

00:17:19.410 --> 00:17:20.010
Got it?

00:17:20.230 --> 00:17:21.430
Yes.

00:17:31.970 --> 00:17:33.070
Sanae...

00:17:37.030 --> 00:17:38.240
Signal confirmed.

00:17:38.240 --> 00:17:41.260
It's the island's high-speed communication
craft, Hayakaze, code Akatsuki.

00:17:41.260 --> 00:17:42.540
Guiding it this way.

00:17:48.750 --> 00:17:50.670
At the moment, that's all we have to report.

00:17:51.270 --> 00:17:52.960
We're changing the island's course.

00:17:53.450 --> 00:17:54.800
There'll be no third expedition.

00:17:55.750 --> 00:17:58.430
Take the whole island out to receive them.

00:18:01.370 --> 00:18:03.690
I'm starving! Is it ready yet?

00:18:03.690 --> 00:18:06.440
There are lots of mouths to feed.
You could help us.

00:18:06.440 --> 00:18:07.470
Yeah, sure.

00:18:08.030 --> 00:18:10.020
Eating with everyone like this is nice.

00:18:10.280 --> 00:18:12.440
Don't your parents live at home with you?

00:18:12.440 --> 00:18:14.060
I always eat alone.

00:18:14.550 --> 00:18:17.530
My parents are busy, and even
if they come home early,

00:18:17.530 --> 00:18:19.030
they just stay in their rooms.

00:18:19.400 --> 00:18:21.260
What? That's weird.

00:18:25.350 --> 00:18:27.410
Saki-san, what is it?

00:18:28.560 --> 00:18:30.420
From the expeditionary force.

00:18:30.690 --> 00:18:33.660
People are living alongside the Mir.

00:18:40.410 --> 00:18:44.500
It's the old well where Emery
received her Mir fragment.

00:18:56.350 --> 00:18:59.610
We've just departed along with 22,000 survivors.

00:19:00.170 --> 00:19:02.340
We don't know what this journey will bring,

00:19:02.340 --> 00:19:05.690
but I'm sure we'll arrive in a land of hope.

00:19:08.680 --> 00:19:12.440
This island really is at peace, isn't it?

00:19:12.440 --> 00:19:14.590
If we lose, the island will go
through the same thing.

00:19:14.590 --> 00:19:17.840
They're idiots, going along with the Human Army.

00:19:17.840 --> 00:19:20.220
That means it's for the island's sake, too.

00:19:20.220 --> 00:19:23.030
In any case, I'm glad they're all safe.

00:19:23.030 --> 00:19:26.160
We'll do everything we can.

00:19:26.160 --> 00:19:28.730
Now, for today, let's get some sleep.

00:19:32.440 --> 00:19:34.230
Reo-chan, are you in here?

00:19:35.090 --> 00:19:36.610
Here. You forgot this.

00:19:37.610 --> 00:19:39.320
Did you look inside?

00:19:39.320 --> 00:19:41.580
Why? Is there something in it?

00:19:42.460 --> 00:19:44.000
There's nothing!

00:19:44.000 --> 00:19:45.120
Mikamika!

00:19:45.120 --> 00:19:47.400
The girls are upstairs. Let's go.

00:19:47.400 --> 00:19:48.350
Okay.

00:19:49.460 --> 00:19:51.210
Goodnight, Reo-chan.

00:19:51.210 --> 00:19:52.370
Y-Yeah.

00:19:54.280 --> 00:19:56.500
I've found myself thinking

00:19:56.500 --> 00:19:58.580
that I can still fight.

00:19:59.380 --> 00:20:01.660
I can't criticize Kazuki now.

00:20:01.660 --> 00:20:03.950
Your batteries are nearly drained, though.

00:20:04.680 --> 00:20:05.390
Our job now

00:20:05.910 --> 00:20:09.900
is to train the new kids.

00:20:11.610 --> 00:20:12.610
You're right.

00:20:37.590 --> 00:20:39.800
Today was a cinch.

00:20:40.710 --> 00:20:42.960
If an enemy came right now, I think I'd lose.

00:20:42.960 --> 00:20:44.800
You need more training.

00:20:48.140 --> 00:20:51.320
If an enemy came right now, I know I'd lose.

00:20:51.320 --> 00:20:52.310
Yeah.

00:20:52.310 --> 00:20:54.250
You need to be more mentally prepared.

00:20:54.250 --> 00:20:56.060
Nah, I think we'd lose.

00:21:02.950 --> 00:21:04.070
How do I look?

00:21:04.070 --> 00:21:06.760
Orihime-chan, what are you doing?

00:21:06.760 --> 00:21:08.680
That's mine...

00:21:10.900 --> 00:21:12.580
Wh-What are you doing?

00:21:12.580 --> 00:21:13.560
It suits you.

00:21:13.560 --> 00:21:15.080
That's mine!

00:21:15.320 --> 00:21:18.210
So soon after a battle, they really
are full of energy.

00:21:26.300 --> 00:21:27.050
What?

00:21:27.620 --> 00:21:29.350
Kondou-sensei, this...

00:21:32.280 --> 00:21:33.250
What is this?

00:21:35.190 --> 00:21:39.250
Rina-senpai, if you sleep here,
you'll catch a cold.

00:21:39.780 --> 00:21:41.230
Come on, Rina-senpai...

00:21:46.330 --> 00:21:47.250
What's wrong?

00:21:50.150 --> 00:21:51.120
The assimilation phenomenon!

00:21:53.350 --> 00:21:54.080
Uh...

00:21:54.080 --> 00:21:54.890
Stop!

00:21:56.650 --> 00:21:57.710
Don't touch anything!

00:22:02.370 --> 00:22:03.230
Rina-senpai?!

00:22:03.230 --> 00:22:04.070
Rina?

00:22:04.830 --> 00:22:06.420
Our human appearances,

00:22:07.790 --> 00:22:08.520
hearts,

00:22:10.210 --> 00:22:11.050
lifestyles...

00:22:13.230 --> 00:22:14.720
You will soon learn that

00:22:15.700 --> 00:22:18.770
we will lose more and more,
as long as we wish for battle.

00:22:21.460 --> 00:22:23.290
We sought the future.

00:22:24.440 --> 00:22:28.750
A future in which we would,
at least, lose one fewer thing.

00:24:05.960 --> 00:24:08.920
<i>Fafner in the Azure: Exodus</i>, episode 12:

00:24:09.530 --> 00:24:11.220
Children of the Battlefield.
